WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:01.980
And such a voice, you know.

2
00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:10.200
I still . . . he was also Tee Jules, he did the Cajun Night Before Christmas, you know when you hear that on the radio?

3
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.620
That’s him.

4
00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:12.760
He didn’t talk like that.

5
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:13.940
That was an accent put on.

6
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.580
The Cajun Twelve Days of Christmas.

7
00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:18.160
I think I still have the single.

8
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.780
He signed it for me, Tee Jules.

9
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:28.540
But, you know when I’m at Christmas Celebration in the Oaks here in New Orleans in City Park they play that.

10
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:33.440
I hear his voice, and I’m starting to tear up now, because I hear his voice even though it’s in a Cajun accent,

11
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.080
(in a deeper voice) and he really had this beautiful accent, talked all the time,

12
00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:39.540
beautiful voice, but then he did the Cajun Night Before Christmas thing.

13
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.920
But I hear his voice and it still makes me weep a little because,

14
00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:47.060
you know . . . And it was just funny because my present day husband is like, “What is wrong with you?

15
00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:47.680
This is funny.

16
00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.400
This is hilarious.”

17
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.060
It’s like, “I know,

18
00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:57.580
but it’s . . . (sniffle) It’s Dr. D.” But that’s the kind of guy he was in the J[ournalism] school and with KLSU.

19
00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:04.620
He was just influential, stern when he needed to be, but a very kind man, very knowledgeable and gave you credit.

20
00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.120
He gave students a lot of respect.

21
00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:08.440
Maybe some didn’t deserve it.

22
00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:13.260
But he let you know that, you know, you knew what you were doing.

23
00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:13.960
And it was nice.
